      "recipeIngredient": [
        "4  - 5  large eggs (2 oz / 57 g in weight (plus more in case any of the eggs crack!))",
        "¾ cup mirin (or Aji mirin)",
        "¼ cup regular soy sauce",
        "¼ cup dark soy sauce",
        "½ cup water",
        "½ tsp cayenne pepper",
        "2 cloves of garlic, or 1 inch piece of ginger (sliced )",
        "1  star anise"
      ],
      "recipeInstructions": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToSection",
          "name": "Ramen eggs",
          "itemListElement": [
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "Fill a large pot with water. Make sure the pot is large enough for the eggs to sit at the bottom in one layer, and for the water level to be about 1 inch above the eggs.",
              "name": "Fill a large pot with water. Make sure the pot is large enough for the eggs to sit at the bottom in one layer, and for the water level to be about 1 inch above the eggs.",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-0-0"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "Add some salt or a little vinegar to the water (this is to prevent the egg whites from leaking out if there are any small cracks while the eggs are cooking).",
              "name": "Add some salt or a little vinegar to the water (this is to prevent the egg whites from leaking out if there are any small cracks while the eggs are cooking).",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-0-1"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "Bring the water to a boil over high heat with the lid on. Then lower the heat to medium or medium high, so that the water is still bubbling but not at a rolling boil (the eggs are more likely to crack at a rolling boil).",
              "name": "Bring the water to a boil over high heat with the lid on. Then lower the heat to medium or medium high, so that the water is still bubbling but not at a rolling boil (the eggs are more likely to crack at a rolling boil).",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-0-2"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "Gently lower each egg into the water. (If any eggs crack while being lowered into the water, I would use them to make omelet or scrambled eggs instead!).",
              "name": "Gently lower each egg into the water. (If any eggs crack while being lowered into the water, I would use them to make omelet or scrambled eggs instead!).",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-0-3"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "As soon as you&#39;ve lowered all the eggs into the water, place the lid back on, and immediately set the timer as follows to cook the eggs to your preference.5 ½ minutes for set, but soft egg whites, and runny egg yolks - these eggs are very delicate.6 minutes for a set white, but runny egg yolk. 6 ½ minutes for a set white, a jammy/runny egg yolk (as seen in the pictures in this post). This is my favorite. 7 minutes for a set white, and a half set egg yolk.",
              "name": "As soon as you&#39;ve lowered all the eggs into the water, place the lid back on, and immediately set the timer as follows to cook the eggs to your preference.5 ½ minutes for set, but soft egg whites, and runny egg yolks - these eggs are very delicate.6 minutes for a set white, but runny egg yolk. 6 ½ minutes for a set white, a jammy/runny egg yolk (as seen in the pictures in this post). This is my favorite. 7 minutes for a set white, and a half set egg yolk.",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-0-4"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "While the eggs are cooking, set up an ice bath for the eggs, or a bowl full of cold tap water in the sink (where the water can be kept running).",
              "name": "While the eggs are cooking, set up an ice bath for the eggs, or a bowl full of cold tap water in the sink (where the water can be kept running).",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-0-5"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "When the time is up, remove the eggs and immediately place them in a bowl with cold running water for at least 2 - 3 minutes, OR place them in the ice bath for a few minutes.",
              "name": "When the time is up, remove the eggs and immediately place them in a bowl with cold running water for at least 2 - 3 minutes, OR place them in the ice bath for a few minutes.",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-0-6"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "Carefully peel the eggs by gently tapping them on a hard surface to create little cracks all over the surface. (The eggs cooked for 5 ½ minutes will be trickier to peel than those cooked for 7 minutes.)",
              "name": "Carefully peel the eggs by gently tapping them on a hard surface to create little cracks all over the surface. (The eggs cooked for 5 ½ minutes will be trickier to peel than those cooked for 7 minutes.)",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-0-7"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "Once peeled, place the eggs in the (cooled) marinade. For those eggs cooked for 5 ½ minutes, put the marinade into a bowl where the eggs can be placed along the bottom in one layer.",
              "name": "Once peeled, place the eggs in the (cooled) marinade. For those eggs cooked for 5 ½ minutes, put the marinade into a bowl where the eggs can be placed along the bottom in one layer.",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-0-8"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "Let the eggs marinate for at least for 2 hours, or 8 - 12 hours for best results, or even up to 24 hours.",
              "name": "Let the eggs marinate for at least for 2 hours, or 8 - 12 hours for best results, or even up to 24 hours.",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-0-9"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "Remove the eggs from the marinade and place them in a separate air-tight container. These can be stored in the fridge for up to 5 days.",
              "name": "Remove the eggs from the marinade and place them in a separate air-tight container. These can be stored in the fridge for up to 5 days.",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-0-10"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "Keep the rest of the marinade in an air-tight container in the fridge. This can be re-used for up to 3 weeks.",
              "name": "Keep the rest of the marinade in an air-tight container in the fridge. This can be re-used for up to 3 weeks.",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-0-11"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToSection",
          "name": "Marinade",
          "itemListElement": [
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "Place the marinade ingredients (except water) in a tall container with an air-tight lid. Whisk to combine (if you added sugar, make sure the sugar is completely dissolved). The basic marinade is now ready.",
              "name": "Place the marinade ingredients (except water) in a tall container with an air-tight lid. Whisk to combine (if you added sugar, make sure the sugar is completely dissolved). The basic marinade is now ready.",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-1-0"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "If you want to infuse the marinade with more flavor, place it in a small saucepan, along with ¼ cup of water. Add chili, or garlic, or ginger, or star anise (or all), and bring the marinade to a simmer. As soon as the sauce starts to simmer, remove it from the heat and let it cool to room temperature.",
              "name": "If you want to infuse the marinade with more flavor, place it in a small saucepan, along with ¼ cup of water. Add chili, or garlic, or ginger, or star anise (or all), and bring the marinade to a simmer. As soon as the sauce starts to simmer, remove it from the heat and let it cool to room temperature.",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-1-1"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "Put the infused marinade in a tall air-tight container, along with the cooked eggs to marinate, as described above.",
              "name": "Put the infused marinade in a tall air-tight container, along with the cooked eggs to marinate, as described above.",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-1-2"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "text": "Add up to ½ cup of water to the marinade if you will be marinating the eggs for longer than 6 hours (in the fridge).",
              "name": "Add up to ½ cup of water to the marinade if you will be marinating the eggs for longer than 6 hours (in the fridge).",
              "url": "https://www.theflavorbender.com/ramen-eggs-ajitsuke-tamago/#wprm-recipe-25982-step-1-3"
            }
          ]
        }
